Subject: wifi: mt76: mt7925: suppress conflicting firmware R4 beacon IEs

The pinned WM 20261016233029 emits DCEA capability zero in autonomous
beacons even while host SDFs advertise pairing/caching and NIRA. iPad
rejects the overwritten capability before PIN entry. Apply the firmware's
NanEnableR4Ie setting before NAN enable, limited to this firmware version.
Air capture confirms beacons retain Master/Cluster attributes without DCEA;
host SDFs retain their security attributes. No firmware binary is modified.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7925/nan.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7925/nan.c
@@ -340,6 +340,18 @@
 
 	if (!vif || !dev || !conf)
 		return -EINVAL;
+
+	/* This WM emits a zero DCEA in its autonomous beacons, overriding
+	 * host-generated pairing/caching capabilities at the peer. Suppress
+	 * firmware R4 IEs; host-generated SDFs retain DCEA and NIRA. The
+	 * fixed firmware is hash-checked by the hardware installation recipe.
+	 */
+	if (!strcmp(dev->mt76.hw->wiphy->fw_version,
+		    "____000000-20261016233029")) {
+		ret = mt7925_mcu_chip_config(dev, "NanEnableR4Ie 0");
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
 
 	skb = mt76_mcu_msg_alloc(mdev, NULL, MT7925_NAN_ENABLE_MAX_SIZE);
 	if (!skb)
